# Project Conventions

**Start with `CLAUDE.md` at the repo root — the stack, the non-negotiables, and
how to find the rule that applies. Read it before making any change.**

Individual conventions are one rule per file in `docs/rules/`, routed by
`docs/rules/INDEX.md`. Read the index, then only the rules that match the file
you are editing — not the whole directory.

This file is a pointer, not a second source, so the copies cannot drift.

## Orientation

| What | Where |
|---|---|
| Coding conventions, patterns, anti-patterns | `CLAUDE.md` |
| Individual rules, one per file — read the index, then only what applies | `docs/rules/INDEX.md` |
| Development lifecycle, gates, sizing rules | `WORKFLOW.md` |
| Workflow commands | `.cursor/commands/` (mirrored from `.claude/commands/`) |
| Index of committed documentation | `.llm/README.md` |
| Design docs · architecture · procedures · QA guides | `docs/plans` · `docs/system` · `docs/sop` · `docs/qa` |

## Non-negotiables

- `bin/test` must pass before claiming anything works
- `bin/rubocop` and `bin/brakeman` must be clean
- Business logic goes in service objects (`ApplicationService`), not controllers
- Slim templates, never ERB, in application views
- Tailwind bracket classes need the `class=""` attribute form — Slim parses `[`
  as attribute syntax
- Fix flaky tests immediately; never skip them
- Update `docs/` when behaviour changes, and grep for an existing doc first
